# NEC2MAA Converter

English | **[简体中文](README.md)**

**A bidirectional antenna-model format converter between NEC and MMANA-GAL** — a pure front-end single-page application that runs by double-clicking (no install, no server, no build chain), developed by BG5TOX.

Converts between the **4NEC2 (.nec/.inp)** and **MMANA-GAL (.maa)** antenna simulation formats. The UI supports runtime switching between **Simplified Chinese and English**.

---

## Quick Start

1. Download/clone this repository anywhere;
2. **Double-click `index.html`** — it opens directly in your browser (file:// protocol; no server or dependencies required);
3. Pick a direction on the start screen (4NEC2 → MMANA-GAL or the reverse), then drop a model file onto the page or use the import button;
4. Review/adjust parameters in the panels, click "Convert";
5. Download the result (automatically named `<original>_converted.maa/.nec`).

> Chrome / Edge recommended. Switch the UI language with the button in the top-right corner; Simplified Chinese is the default and your choice is remembered by the browser.

---

## Main Features

### Direction 1: 4NEC2 (.nec) → MMANA-GAL (.maa)

**NEC-2 cards supported on the input side:**

| Category | Cards | Handling |
|---|---|---|
| Geometry | `GW` (straight wire), `GX` (mirror), `GM` (rotate/translate/copy) | Single pass in file order; GM implements the full multi-axis rotation matrix and NRPT copy semantics |
| Geometry (warned passthrough) | `GA` `GH` `GR` `SP` `SM` | Not convertible — a clear warning is raised and manual review is advised |
| Excitation | `EX 0/5/6` | Mapped to an MMANA voltage source; EX 6 current sources are mapped numerically with a warning; EX 1–4 (plane-wave/point sources) have no equivalent — dropped with a warning |
| Loads | `LD 1/2/3/4/5` | Series RLC / parallel RLC (single-frequency equivalent) / series impedance / parallel admittance (exact) / conductivity (manual setup hint); LD 0/6/7 rejected and preserved as comments |
| Environment | `GN` (all four ground types), `FR` (sweeps take F1) | GN 2 (Sommerfeld-Norton) is downgraded to MININEC real ground with a warning |
| Symbols | `SY` (one per card), `GS` (scaling incl. mm/cm/m/in/ft unit suffixes) | Safe expression evaluation with SIN/COS/TAN/SQRT/ABS/EXP/LOG/PI and uH/nF/pF unit literals |
| Comments | `CM`/`CE` | Kept in the output comment section (pure-ASCII gate) |

**Output .maa characteristics:** dual-variant detection; wire radii/coordinates converted to metres; source/load rows use the MMANA manual designator syntax (`w?c/b/e±offset`); auto-segmentation parameters (DM1/DM2/SC/EC) and the full 7-field G/H line (ground / additional height / material index / impedance / F-B statistics range); unsupported structures (TL transmission lines, etc.) are clearly warned about and appended to the comment tail.

### Direction 2: MMANA-GAL (.maa) → 4NEC2 (.nec)

**.maa characteristics supported on the input side:**

- **Both file variants** (A compact count-line / B per-section headers), including the Russian single-star section headers (`* Провода *`) — sections are classified by data shape, immune to CP1251 mojibake;
- **CP1251 encoding auto-detection:** .maa files saved by the Russian MMANA build are re-decoded as windows-1251 when the UTF-8 trial decode yields replacement characters;
- **Wires/sources/loads:** 8-field wire rows, `w?c/b/e±offset` designator sources (phase/magnitude), and both load forms (series L-C-Q / fixed R-jX impedance);
- **`$$$ Taper wire set $$$` tapered elements (this project's core contribution):** negative-radius wires are **rebuilt into multiple connected GW sub-sections with stepped radii** per the definition table — fully implementing both symmetric (center-out) and sequential expansion semantics, the tip sentinel (L≥99999), center-node cross-midpoint merging, and 50% feedpoint anchoring (see `docs/MAA format concise reference.md` §5a for the full semantics, verified by user-supplied formulas);
- **Segmentation / G/H parameters, ###Comment### text** (non-ASCII content dropped per policy with an aggregate warning).

**Output .nec characteristics:** CM English summary header (original title / provenance / taper rebuild / material hints); SY symbol cards, one per card (radii as descending D1..Dn, load L/C/Q, base symbols f/h); GW radius `0.5*Dn` expressions and `z+h` vertical offset; EX **percentage anchoring** (`50%`/`1`/`100%`) with precise tapered sub-section positioning (e.g. `29, 43.2%`); LD expressions (`2*PI*f*L1*1E-6/Q1`); all four GN ground-type mappings (with σ/εr panel input and 27 presets sourced from 4NEC2's Ground.txt); FR frequency; **output is enforced pure ASCII** (terminal assertion).

### General

- Drag-and-drop or button import, automatic direction switching by file extension, automatic sniffing of pasted .maa text;
- Every parameter panel is editable before conversion (frequency / impedance / axis swap / ground / segmentation density / sources / loads / title mode);
- Every semantic that cannot be mapped exactly produces a **numbered warning** (on-screen in the current UI language; written to the output file always in English);
- Language-pack architecture: adding a language means copying one file under `js/i18n/` (see "Extending" below).

