## Referenced External Projects

| Project | Use |
|---|---|
| **[MMANA-GAL](http://www.gal-ana.de/basicmm/)** (Alexandre Schewelew et al.) | Defines the .maa format (official manual); the official example library (722 files) serves as the full regression corpus for parsing and conversion |
| **4NEC2** (Arie Voors) | The .nec working baseline; its Ground.txt preset table (27 soil entries) was transcribed as the M2N ground-preset dropdown |
| **OpenNEC** / NEC-2 documentation | Reference for the GM rotation matrix (order R = Rz·Ry·Rx); several field-semantic errors in its .maa format description were corrected by this project's census (see `docs/MAA file format (corrected).md`) |
| MMANA-GAL official ANT library (722 files) + community antenna collections (935 files) | The census basis for .maa variants/designators/load forms/taper-block distribution (the format reference is written from full censuses) |
| W8BYA Collinear 7 MHz, jp2000_147.maa and other community models | Gold-standard regression samples |

> This is an independent tool, not affiliated with MMANA-GAL / 4NEC2 / OpenNEC; all names and trademarks belong to their respective authors.

